    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39333" root="نثر" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُرٌّ مَنْثُورٌ</span></b> , and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَثِيرٌ</span></b> , <i>Pearls scattered, strewn,
dispersed,</i> or <i>thrown dispersedly, with the hand.</i>
(A, * TA.) See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُنْتَثِرٌ</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُنَثَّرٌ</span>. You say
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَأَنَّ لَفْظَهُ الدُّرُّ النَّثِيرُ</span></b>  [<i>As though his speech were
scattered pearls</i>]. (A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَهُ كَرِشٌ مَنْثُورَةٌ</span> (tropical:)  <i>He
has</i> [<i>numerous</i>] <i>young children.</i> (A, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كرش</span>.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنْثُورٌ</span> <i>A kind of sweet-smelling flower;</i>
(TA;) [the <i>gilliflower:</i> so called in the present
day: see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خِيرِىٌّ</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَشْخَاشٌ</span>.

